# Code review checklist — SQL migrations

Before merging a Supabase migration, walk this list. Deeper guidance lives in the `project-supabase` skill and `supabase-security.mdc`.

## RLS

- Every new user-facing table **enables RLS** in this migration.
- Policies are present for the operations you actually need (`select`, `insert`, `update`, `delete`) — and **only** those.
- No `USING (true)` / `WITH CHECK (true)` on user data in production. If a broad policy is required (e.g. service-role-only access), document **why** in the migration.

```sql
-- GOOD: scoped to the owning user
create policy "trips_select_own" on trips
  for select to authenticated
  using (organizer_id = auth.uid());
```

## Money privacy (ADR 0002 hard rule)

If this migration touches a **money table** (`expenses`, `expense_shares`, `payouts`, or anything monetary):

- Select / insert / update policies are **members-only** (membership-based), and **do not** consult `trips.visibility`, `follows`, or any other social-grant table.
- No branch fans out money rows to non-members regardless of the trip's `visibility` value.
- A public Trip exposes its itinerary, photos, and Posts; it **never** exposes amounts.
- If the feature requires a public money-shaped surface (rare), it lives in a **separate denormalized table** with its own narrow policy — not as a relaxation of the policy on the underlying money table. That relaxation needs a new ADR.

See [`supabase-security.mdc`](supabase-security.mdc) → "Money data is never readable by non-trip-members" for the hard rule and the GOOD/BAD examples.

## Image pre-moderation (ADR 0002 hard rule)

If this migration touches `images`, `posts`, `profiles` (avatar column), or any new table that holds user-uploaded image references:

- The image row carries an `image_state` enum (`pending_review` | `approved` | `rejected`) — or its parent post/profile column equivalent.
- The select policy gates non-owner, non-moderator reads on `state = 'approved'`. Pending and rejected images are visible only to the uploader and the moderator role.
- Storage paths reflect the two-tier model: `images-pending/...` (private bucket) for non-approved files, `images-approved/...` (public-readable) for approved files. New tables / columns should align with this.
- The **EXIF GPS strip + CSAM scan** server-side pipeline runs before any image row enters `pending_review`. Migrations that add an upload path without referencing this pipeline fail review.
- Posts whose photos are not yet approved sit in their own `pending_media` / `pending_review` state and are not visible in any feed.

See [`supabase-security.mdc`](supabase-security.mdc) → "Every uploaded image is pre-moderated and invisible until approved" for the hard rule and the GOOD/BAD examples.

## Indexes

- Columns referenced in RLS predicates and common query filters (`user_id`, `trip_id`, FK columns) have an index.
- Don't over-index: every index has a query that justifies it. Note the query in the migration comment when not obvious.

## Dangerous patterns

- No `DROP TABLE` / `DROP COLUMN` without an explicit data-preservation plan in the PR description.
- No `ALTER TABLE` that rewrites a large table without a migration strategy.
- No `GRANT ALL` to `anon` or `authenticated`; grants are minimal and intentional.
- No raw user input concatenated into dynamic SQL — use parameter binding everywhere.

## Reversibility / safety

- Destructive operations are gated behind a clear, named migration (so rollback is obvious).
- Foreign keys have an `on delete` policy that matches product intent (don't default to silent cascade for financial data).

If any item fails, **fix it now or file a Bead** — do not merge.
